abstract="Process calculi based in logic, such as {\$}{\$}{\backslash}uppi {\$}{\$}DILL and CP, provide a foundation for deadlock-free concurrent programming, but exclude non-determinism and races. {\$}{\$}{\backslash}text {\{}HCP{\}}{\$}{\$}is a reformulation of CP which addresses a fundamental shortcoming: the fundamental operator for parallel composition from the {\$}{\$}{\backslash}uppi {\$}{\$}-calculus does not correspond to any rule of linear logic, and therefore not to any term construct in CP.",
